+Each **Truck** cell has a right-aligned **⇄** button (**F4** or **Alt+Down** when focused) that opens the replacement comparison popup. Its candidates use the same enabled base-game/owned-DLC catalog as Tier list, regardless of Tier list groups or filters. Class and default-tire filters combine; column headers sort the list. The popup uses the shared double-Shift search with a three-character minimum to search all displayed strings and attached metadata. Selecting a candidate updates the resizable lower comparison table: current map equipment versus candidate defaults, internal component names, nonvisual installed addons, vehicle properties, compatible wheel families/tires and nonvisual addon socket options. Truck/Class/Truck ID rows and detailed engine, gearbox, suspension and winch settings are omitted from the comparison. Socket options shared by both trucks are always hidden, independently of the Differences only checkbox. The comparison uses an animated pixel-scrolling viewport instead of jumping by variable-height rows; wheel input over the table, keyboard navigation and shared search all use this viewport. Changed values are highlighted, with a **Differences only** checkbox. Socket matches alone do not validate addon conflicts or other restrictions; explicit definition values do not fully resolve templates. The **Apply replacement** button saves the selected model with its default addons and default engine/gearbox/winch/suspension/wheels. Placement ID, transform and all bytes outside the model/equipment fields are preserved. The button is disabled for the current model, during saving, and after a successful save. Saved and backup paths are displayed; closing the popup reloads Regions-Trucks from the edited map.
 
 The catalog matches placement IDs to nested task/contract settings in the active workspace. Explicit `REWARD` actions indicate obtainable task vehicles; `DESTROY` and `mustDestroyAfterSubstage` indicate mission-only vehicles. Untagged world placements are labeled **Obtainable — discovery/start**, an inference that includes starting vehicles. Named placements without an explicit ownership rule, and conflicting reward/removal rules, remain **Unverified**. Classification evidence, map coordinates and source metadata remain available internally for search. This is a catalog of the selected map files, not the player's save progress. Use a workspace from the same game version as the maps. Reading does not modify or extract the source archives.
 
